Don't fire an unidentified wand into a closet; it could bounce back
(if it's one of the types that does so) and hit you (and wands of this
type generally either do a fair amount of damage or just kill you
outright, if you don't have the appropriate protection). If you must
test a wand by firing it, fire it at an angle, or down a corridor
known to be fairly long.

Aiming the wand down with > should be safe. Having found out that you
had a wand of digging, you could use it to get away from those
monsters by zapping down. (If you get stuck in a pit, just try again.)
Wands normally have several charges to start with (unless e.g. a
monster has used them up).

Also, not every character class is meant to take on every combat
challenge head-on, especially at the beginning. Being in a corridor
(from zapping the wand of digging) helps, though (since they are
forced to come at you one at a time instead of swarming).

